# ── Secrets and machine-local state — never commit ──────────────
config.json
state.json
*.lock
.env
.env.*
*.token
*.pem
*.key

# ── Working correspondence — carries live credentials ───────────
# Docs/ holds the build prompts and replies. Those have already carried
# the monitor_ro SQL password and, in ksjud7.md, the Supabase JWT secret
# and service_role key. Structural exclusion, not a habit of remembering.
Docs/

# ── Customer data — real sales, employees, and cash counts ──────
# Kept local on purpose. The GitHub Actions runner checks out this
# repo; the customer's raw POS data must never land there.
data UN/

# ── Built artefact — never committed ────────────────────────────
# ship/ is assembled by make_ship.py from the files in this repository.
# Committing a second copy of agent.py is precisely how the customer
# machine ends up running code that drifted from the tests months ago.
# Rebuild it, do not store it.
ship/

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ── Editors / OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── The release artifact — built, never committed ───────────────
# `python make_ship.py --zip` produces this from ship/. It is what the
# operator downloads, and it carries MANIFEST.txt so a ZIP install is
# integrity-checked exactly like a clone. Attach it to a GitHub Release;
# committing it would be a second copy of the code, which is the whole
# thing ship/ exists to avoid.
posentine-*.zip
